    "created_at": "2020-08-07T14:49:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-07T14:49:35Z",
    "body": "I agree that this is not like other defaults. But I think that's OK.\r\n\r\nAnother way to think about it is to realize how weird the current `optional` keyword is. In `foo(boolean abc = false)`, the `abc` argument is \"optional\": the web developer doesn't have to pass it in. But we don't use the `optional` keyword for that---because it's redundant with the default value. Similarly, if we can use `undefined` as a default value, then adding the `optional` keyword becomes redundant for the `foo(DOMString abc = undefined)` case.\r\n\r\nIn other words, it is good to align the case of \"allows no argument and gets a default value of `false`\" with \"allows no argument and gets a default value of `undefined`\".",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/670554790/reactions",
